# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Referrer-Policy sends the origin and never the path. A blanket no-referrer
# was tried first and OpenStreetMap refused every tile with 403, because its
# usage policy requires an identifiable client. The origin is safe to send:
# Locus never puts a coordinate in a URL, so there is no path to leak, and the
# one request that carries a coordinate sets referrerPolicy: 'no-referrer'
# itself in src/api.ts.
#
# Permissions-Policy proves the v0.1 claim that geolocation is not used -- the
# browser refuses the API even if some future dependency asks for it.
/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
